# Password Policy Audit

## Overview

The **Password Policy Audit** module examines password-related security settings to help administrators verify that user authentication policies follow recommended security practices. It reviews password aging policies, password hashing algorithms, account expiration, and account lockout settings to identify configurations that may increase the risk of unauthorized access.

Strong password policies are a fundamental component of system security. Weak or misconfigured policies can make user accounts more vulnerable to password guessing, brute-force attacks, and credential compromise.

