# Common Attack Scenarios

## Brute-Force Attack

An attacker repeatedly attempts different passwords against a user account.

Without an account lockout policy, the attacker may eventually guess the correct password.

---

## Weak Password Hashes

An attacker obtains a copy of `/etc/shadow`.

Weak hashing algorithms significantly reduce the time required for offline password-cracking attacks.

---

## Never-Expiring Passwords

An employee continues using the same password for several years.

If the password is leaked through another service, attackers may reuse it to access the system.

---

## Disabled Password Policy

A newly deployed server uses default authentication settings without password aging or account lockout protection.

The system becomes more susceptible to credential attacks.

