# How the Toolkit Implements These Checks

High-level workflow:

```text
Read password policy configuration

            │

            ▼

Check password aging settings

            │

            ▼

Identify hashing algorithm

            │

            ▼

Detect expired passwords

            │

            ▼

Verify account lockout policy

            │

            ▼

Generate findings
```

The toolkit performs read-only inspections using standard Linux utilities and does not modify any authentication settings.

---

# Expected Findings

A properly configured Linux system should typically have:

- Password aging enabled.
- Reasonable password expiration settings.
- A modern password hashing algorithm.
- No unexpected expired passwords.
- Account lockout protection enabled.

